1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,920
Tsuruno is the strongest.

2
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:09,320
She's stronger than everyone.

3
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:12,680
And since she's so strong, she's okay.

4
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:15,400
Tsuruno, stop.

5
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:18,760
I am the strongest.

6
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:22,060
What happened, Yachiyo? Are you okay?

7
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:25,040
She rejected my connect.

8
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:28,020
You're kidding. But how come?

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,320
What the heck happened?

10
00:00:32,180 --> 00:00:34,060
Was our timing off or something?

11
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:36,040
I don't know.

12
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:40,600
But I think it's good we stopped our attack when we did.

13
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,580
Now what are we supposed to do?

14
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:49,680
Don't worry. I will save everyone.

15
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:52,320
I think we should get going.

16
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:57,960
Uh-oh.

17
00:00:57,960 --> 00:00:59,960
What did we do?

18
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:05,740
Tsuruno is one of the Magius's best creations.

19
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:07,800
How dare they treat her so rough?

20
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:09,560
Those darn poop heads.

21
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:12,240
Now I'm really, really, really mad.

22
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:14,060
Toka.

23
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:19,280
Why do things turn out like this?

24
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:25,520
She's strong.

25
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:28,460
The strongest magical girl ever.

26
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:30,880
That's why she's not hurt.

27
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:32,620
She's A-OK.

28
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:37,080
Yachiyo, try connecting again.

29
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:39,040
Sorry.

30
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:40,460
I can't.

31
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:41,440
Huh?

32
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:43,760
I can't.

33
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:46,680
I guess I didn't know her after all.

34
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,400
But you know her the best!

35
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:49,920
I don't.

36
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:51,940
I never really knew her.

37
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:54,040
I don't think she'll cause the second one to 21 Ran.

38
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:55,340
Who's there?

39
00:01:55,580 --> 00:01:56,180
Okay.

40
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:58,600
I mean, it's not far too much.

41
00:01:58,680 --> 00:01:59,860
He's funny.

42
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:04,800
I know she says.

43
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:41,080
At the start, I had a feeling our plan wasn't going to work.

44
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:47,040
Where is this?

45
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:53,760
I told myself I knew Tsuruno, and I thought I did, but I didn't.

46
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:59,240
Yachiyo? What's wrong? Yachiyo!

47
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:06,840
Deep down, I knew the truth. I didn't know or understand Tsuruno at all.

48
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:13,200
I refused to admit it to myself. I completely shut it out.

49
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:22,100
I guess the reason was I didn't want to be right, and so I chose the kind of person I wanted her to be.

50
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:25,200
I... I didn't bother learning who she was.

51
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:31,900
I'm Tsuruno Yui, the magical girl. The strongest.

52
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:33,320
Tsuruno?

53
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:39,340
I always act cheerful and energetic, because that's who I have to be.

54
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:42,640
That's right, I have to be that girl.

55
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:46,020
I've had to be that girl.

56
00:04:47,660 --> 00:04:48,600
That day.

57
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:56,780
According to my fortune, today is going to be the luckiest day of my life. Really?

58
00:04:57,280 --> 00:05:00,660
Hold on. You promised you wouldn't tell any more fortunes, Mel.

59
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:05,380
Your predictions always end up being accurate. So if the result is unfavorable...

60
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:09,980
Hey, this is that past event I saw in the Memory Museum.

61
00:05:09,980 --> 00:05:14,780
If she gets a bad result, then we'll just work hard to stop it.

62
00:05:16,940 --> 00:05:18,360
Here you go, folks!

63
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:22,280
One large Mopo sweet and sour pork! It's Bon Bon's eye specialty!

64
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:25,300
Hey there, Master!

65
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:28,380
Hi, Tsuruno. You free?

66
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:30,760
Yeah, only for a couple seconds.

67
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:33,360
We're packed today, like super busy!

68
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:37,860
Uh, well, we just spotted a witch that came here from Daito Ward.

69
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:45,320
But I'm here with everyone already.

70
00:05:45,940 --> 00:05:48,820
So if you can't come, it's okay. We'll handle it.

71
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:54,000
I'm sorry. It's rare for us to get a reservation for such a large group.

72
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:57,040
No. Stay and help your parents.

73
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:59,760
Thanks a lot, Master Yachiyo.

74
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:05,260
I believed her, so I stayed at work and didn't help with that witch.

75
00:06:11,260 --> 00:06:13,960
Mel died? For real?

76
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:18,980
But, like, you said you guys could handle it.

77
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:22,840
I know, but the witch was too strong.

78
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:27,180
It's my fault. I should've gone.

79
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:30,020
What? No. It was bad luck.

80
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:34,460
If I'd have been there with them, Mel wouldn't have died.

81
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:36,500
There's nothing we could do.

82
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:39,760
If you were there, it wouldn't have changed anything.

83
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:44,200
They don't think I'm strong enough to matter.

84
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:46,920
Don't blame yourself for it, Tsuruno.

85
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:49,080
It's no one's fault.

86
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:56,120
It's my fault for being weak.

87
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:59,640
Mel was killed because I'm weak.

88
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:02,880
No, Tsuruno! That's not true!

89
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:10,440
I have to get stronger.

90
00:07:13,240 --> 00:07:14,280
I failed.

91
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:17,000
So now, I must get stronger.

92
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:20,500
Mel was killed because I was weak.

93
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:21,920
That's not true!

94
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:25,760
I just heard Mifuyu's missing!

95
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:27,280
It's true.

96
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:29,840
She's not answering my calls.

97
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:34,960
I still had so much I wanted to learn from Mifuyu, too.

98
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:40,440
Why do I have to protect Senkyo Ward on my own?

99
00:07:41,060 --> 00:07:43,680
Because Momoko's training new magical girls.

100
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:52,280
If there's anything you need to know about magical girls, just hit me up.

101
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:54,280
Thanks, Momoko. You're the best!

102
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,940
Even Momoko doesn't want to be around me.

103
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:03,000
If you think it's too much for you...

104
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:07,340
Not even Master Gachiyo!

105
00:08:07,340 --> 00:08:10,380
I'm the strongest magical girl, so I can handle anything!

106
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:12,920
I have to.

107
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:14,600
I don't have a choice.

108
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:17,300
I have to be the strongest magical girl.

109
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:19,000
Otherwise...

110
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:22,720
Everyone's going to turn their backs on me.

111
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:29,500
I have to work harder.

112
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:32,440
I can't complain about the strain.

113
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:37,720
If they see I'm worried about something, they'll stop trusting me.

114
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:41,080
I'm Tsuda-no the magical girl.

115
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:44,600
I'm always cheerful and energetic and strong.

116
00:08:51,060 --> 00:08:52,160
Are you okay?

117
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:59,860
That was nothing! I could do this all day!

118
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:05,740
I can't count on Yachiyo anymore.

119
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:11,660
Even if she says I can sit this fight out, I can't trust her.

120
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:13,860
I've got loads of energy to spare!

121
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:16,700
That's why I'll always win!

122
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:31,480
I'm the strongest.

123
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:38,480
And now, I'm wondering how long I have to keep acting this way.

124
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:51,480
A customer!

125
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:54,480
Welcome to Chinese Restaurant Bon Banzai!

126
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:59,480
I need to be an example to all the other magical girls in Kamehama.

127
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:03,480
More cheerful, more energetic.

128
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:06,480
I need to be the strongest of them all.

129
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:08,480
None of that stuff matters.

130
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:10,480
Be yourself and that's enough!

131
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:17,480
I have to work harder.

132
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:21,480
I have to work harder.

133
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:23,480
I have to work harder!

134
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:31,480
You and your fortunes!

135
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:33,480
What part of this is lucky?

136
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:35,480
This is awful!

137
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,480
It's not!

138
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:40,480
I am lucky!

139
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:42,480
I have to work harder.

140
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:48,480
Wait, is this...?

141
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:50,480
Oh no...

142
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:54,480
This is when I...

143
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:55,480
I...

144
00:10:58,480 --> 00:10:59,480
No!

145
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:02,480
Saruna, it's not what you think!

146
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:03,480
It's not!

147
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:13,480
I can't put up this front anymore.

148
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:14,480
I don't want to.

149
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:17,480
I'm done.

150
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:20,480
I don't have anything left to offer.

151
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:21,480
I...

152
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,480
You're wrong, you too!

153
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:29,480
Now I know what went wrong.

154
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:32,480
It's my fault.

155
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:34,480
I put too much pressure on her.

156
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:35,480
Yachiyo!

157
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:51,480
That was weird...

158
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:52,480
Wasn't it?

159
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:55,480
The Kinect linked us with her subconscious...

160
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:00,480
Fino's the strongest magical girl!

161
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:02,480
They stronger than anyone!

162
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:03,480
Anyone!

163
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:04,480
You can stop now!

164
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:05,480
We know the truth!

165
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:06,480
Wake up!

166
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:08,480
She's strong and she's okay!

167
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:11,480
She's just fine!

168
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:18,480
You're not okay at all!

169
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:20,480
Felicia...

170
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:21,480
You're not as strong as you say!

171
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:23,480
So quit lying already!

172
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:26,480
Quit hiding how you really feel!

173
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,480
Be honest!

174
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:29,480
You're gonna kill yourself if you're not!

175
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:31,480
Felicia...

176
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:32,480
Stay back!

177
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:33,480
Oh, shut up!

178
00:12:33,480 --> 00:12:34,480
You're the same as her!

179
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:39,480
I admit it.

180
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:41,480
It's my fault she's suffering.

181
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:44,480
I pushed her to get stronger and stronger.

182
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:48,480
I put the pressure on her that led to this.

183
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:49,480
Or...

184
00:12:51,480 --> 00:13:04,480
It'll get closer to it...

185
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:09,480
Or...

186
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:14,040
Maybe you were, but you weren't even tougher on yourself.

187
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:17,780
But nobody's so strong they can go it alone.

188
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:24,740
Ask yourself this, how do you want Sudono to be from now on?

189
00:13:29,620 --> 00:13:33,740
All I want is for her to stop pretending.

190
00:13:33,740 --> 00:13:40,880
Alone, we're not strong enough, but together we are.

191
00:13:41,380 --> 00:13:41,980
Iroha.

192
00:13:46,980 --> 00:13:48,940
Could someone please help?

193
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:53,000
Looks like I made it right on time.

194
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:54,320
Momoku!

195
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:56,860
Ugh, don't be ridiculous.

196
00:13:58,460 --> 00:14:00,520
You barely made it in time.

197
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:01,620
Nifuyu!

198
00:14:01,620 --> 00:14:04,360
We can keep the witches off your back.

199
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:06,260
Now go and save Sudono.

200
00:14:11,980 --> 00:14:12,420
Sudono!

201
00:14:20,420 --> 00:14:21,660
Hurry, take the shot!

202
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:36,600
Let's connect and bring her back.

203
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:37,580
Right.

204
00:14:37,580 --> 00:14:46,260
I know you never wanted to be the strongest of us, but you never had to be.

205
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:48,960
There were enough of us to share the burden.

206
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:53,580
Remember, we're always here for you and ready to listen.

207
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:56,420
I'm sorry, Sudono.

208
00:14:56,420 --> 00:14:57,280
Let's começa.

209
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:16,300
Huh.

210
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:26,660
Come on, it's our turn.

211
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:33,860
Out of us all, Mommy is the strongest and always took the time to teach us.

212
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:35,920
But she pushed herself too hard.

213
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:38,460
I failed, I failed everyone.

214
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:40,680
Now it's up to me to save them.

215
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:43,160
She's busted out! Hurry!

216
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:48,900
We want our Mommy back!

217
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:54,440
Time to come back to us, Mommy!

218
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:56,620
Kiro, do it!

219
00:16:10,540 --> 00:16:11,740
We did it!

220
00:16:16,300 --> 00:16:19,460
We're up!

221
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:20,340
Right!

222
00:16:21,080 --> 00:16:21,640
Head out!

223
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:27,140
The Witches are leaving.

224
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:48,060
The Witches are leaving.

225
00:16:48,060 --> 00:16:55,800
It worked!

226
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,400
We make a good team, huh?

227
00:16:58,200 --> 00:16:59,620
You can be such a pain.

228
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:03,180
Thanks, everyone. I'm sorry.

229
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:06,360
We're glad you're back.

230
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:10,080
Yachiyo?

231
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:11,360
Just relax.

232
00:17:11,860 --> 00:17:13,480
Are you okay, Tsuruno?

233
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:14,280
Yeah.

234
00:17:15,020 --> 00:17:16,460
I'm sorry, guys.

235
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:20,120
You don't need to apologize.

236
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:22,440
I'm sorry, Tsuruno.

237
00:17:24,040 --> 00:17:26,400
Felicia, I'm sorry for everything.

238
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:28,340
O-okay.

239
00:17:29,340 --> 00:17:30,580
Don't feel bad.

240
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:33,360
Seriously, everyone makes mistakes.

241
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:35,080
Fixing them's all that matters.

242
00:17:35,760 --> 00:17:36,880
Yes, you're right.

243
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:43,240
Momoko, Mifuyu, thank you for helping bring Tsuruno back to us.

244
00:17:44,420 --> 00:17:47,900
It doesn't even begin to make up for what I've done.

245
00:17:49,160 --> 00:17:53,640
The important thing is, we're together again, and that's all that matters.

246
00:17:59,640 --> 00:18:02,220
Together again? This is great!

247
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:07,860
The violent winds that slammed into Kamehama have finally subsided.

248
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:10,040
The supercell is still active, though.

249
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:13,560
It has changed course and is now heading straight for Mitakihara.

250
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:15,820
Oh no.

251
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:18,120
Valpurgis Noct is heading for our town.

252
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:20,600
We have to get back home.

253
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:24,980
But she can't be there when Valpurgis Noct arrives.

254
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:26,720
Come on, let's go.

255
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:27,220
What?

256
00:18:27,220 --> 00:18:41,080
Iroha.

257
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:46,540
I hope you find your friends and get through to them.

258
00:18:46,540 --> 00:19:07,900
I better hurry.

259
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,600
What the heck?

260
00:19:14,060 --> 00:19:15,660
Are you feeling better?

261
00:19:15,660 --> 00:19:16,900
Oh yeah.

262
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:19,140
Way better than before, for sure.

263
00:19:20,940 --> 00:19:21,460
Iroha.

264
00:19:29,980 --> 00:19:32,480
Do you really think they are going to accept you?

265
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:36,400
You're way different from them, you know.

266
00:19:39,220 --> 00:19:42,940
Remember, when I was weak, you offered to give me a hand?

267
00:19:42,940 --> 00:19:43,120
I don't.

268
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:43,180
I don't.

269
00:19:45,180 --> 00:19:46,180
But I...

270
00:19:46,180 --> 00:19:48,180
I want...

271
00:19:48,180 --> 00:19:51,320
To go with them, you can't.

272
00:19:58,320 --> 00:19:59,580
You're different.

273
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:03,400
They're nothing like you.

274
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:18,280
I don't need to be strong to beat these things.

275
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:21,920
That's it.

276
00:20:31,520 --> 00:20:32,000
Telka!

277
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:34,740
Iroha Tamaki!

278
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:35,960
Talk to me.

279
00:20:36,420 --> 00:20:37,900
Tell me why you're doing this.

280
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:40,160
I don't have to tell you a darn thing, darn it.

281
00:20:40,260 --> 00:20:42,540
I had an amazing plan and you ruined it!

282
00:20:42,540 --> 00:20:43,920
But your plan was horrible.

283
00:20:44,420 --> 00:20:45,320
Kidnapping people?

284
00:20:45,500 --> 00:20:46,520
Destroying the town?

285
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:47,600
Honestly!

286
00:20:47,940 --> 00:20:49,460
Like I keep telling everyone,

287
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:51,800
it was the only way to save us magical girls!

288
00:20:52,580 --> 00:20:53,640
I know you.

289
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:56,020
You're not the kind of girl who would do this.

290
00:20:56,020 --> 00:21:00,400
What do you mean you know me?

291
00:21:01,140 --> 00:21:02,480
Who do you think you are?

292
00:21:04,480 --> 00:21:07,040
Toka, enough is enough.

293
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:09,640
Nemuro!

294
00:21:10,300 --> 00:21:11,620
Hey, big sis.

295
00:21:12,140 --> 00:21:13,360
I've missed you.

296
00:21:14,420 --> 00:21:15,480
Big sis?

297
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:18,740
You mean you know this person, Nemuro?

298
00:21:19,100 --> 00:21:20,280
No, we do.

299
00:21:21,140 --> 00:21:23,520
I'm sorry, but I've been lying to you.

300
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:29,660
But now, there's no reason to hide the truth from everyone anymore.

301
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:38,320
What are you doing?

302
00:21:39,560 --> 00:21:42,600
It's time I told both of you the truth.

303
00:21:43,320 --> 00:21:44,820
The truth about us.

304
00:21:45,380 --> 00:21:47,120
And everything that's happened.

305
00:21:53,520 --> 00:22:14,960
The truth about us.

